+# Thor aarch64 (BLENDER_PLATFORM_ARM): build CPU-only OSL, i.e. leave OSL_USE_OPTIX at its
+# upstream default of OFF. The OptiX/CUDA shadeops path compiles OSL's shadeops to PTX via
+# clang (LLVM_COMPILE_CUDA), which on CUDA 13 + our clang 17 breaks inside the CUDA runtime
+# header texture_fetch_functions.h. It is also useless here: Jetson has no OptiX runtime,
+# Blender is built WITH_CYCLES_DEVICE_OPTIX=OFF, and Cycles on the CUDA (non-OptiX) device
